  "statement": "K = (A_m x A_m) \u22ca C_2 = A_m wr C_2 < S_{2m}; (U,V) acts by U on {0..m-1}, V on {m..2m-1}; sigma: j -> j+m mod 2m. x = (U,V)\u00b7sigma, a = (B,A), c = (U',V')\u00b7sigma.  Then x a x^2 = c  <=>  (U'=UAVU and V'=VBUV). Every solution in K lies in the sigma-coset (sigma-exponent of x a x^2 is that of x). a = 1 <=> A = B = id: cube root. Also a x^3 = x^-1 c x, hence ctype(a x^3) = ctype(c) and x^3 = (UVU, VUV)\u00b7sigma.",
